  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "As Culling Dais's last ability resolves, its last existence on the battlefield is checked to determine how many charge counters were on it.",
      "oracle_id": "42b03dd7-e796-47c3-b596-87960d72818b",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As Golden Urn\u2019s last ability resolves, its last existence on the battlefield is checked to determine how many charge counters were on it.",
      "oracle_id": "ddb19cac-20b0-4ab8-a31d-c5c155491780",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If enough -1/-1 counters are put on Bloodtracker at the same time to make its toughness 0 or less, the number of +1/+1 counters on it before it got any -1/-1 counters will be used to determine how many cards you draw. For example, if there are three +1/+1 counters on Bloodtracker and it gets six -1/-1 counters, you'll draw three cards. That's because Bloodtracker's triggered ability checks the creature's existence just before it leaves the battlefield, and it still has all those counters on it at that point.",
      "oracle_id": "fcf9ced2-867d-4bc5-b7b6-6153ed2cac97",
      "published_at": "2018-07-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
